**What was wrong:** The `pip` package files had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, but the pip entry-point scripts at `/usr/local/bin/pip` and `/usr/local/bin/pip3` remained, along with a stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory. When you ran `pip`, it tried to `import pip` and failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`.

**What I did:**
1. Removed the leftover `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory
2. Ran `python -m ensurepip --upgrade` to reinstall the pip package properly
3. Verified pip works by installing `requests` successfully

Your pip is now fully functional.

